<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Every Jawa pawn kind rolls `MandrakeJawa`. Owner's ruling 2026-08-14: it is the
    ONLY active Jawa xenotype.

    🔴 THIS IS A WORLDGEN GATE, NOT A TUNING PATCH. `xenotypeSet` is read at PAWN
    GENERATION, so a patch landing after a world exists does not fix that world's
    colonists — you get a campaign whose Jawas are quietly the wrong xenotype on a
    desert planet, and nothing errors.

    🔴 RETARGETED 2026-08-19 (B58). This file used to patch Outer Rim's
    `OuterRim_Jawa` and `OuterRim_JawaTribal`. Switching the three donor mods off
    and `mandrake.starwarsraces` on DELETED both — measured against the live def
    dump, neither name resolves as a PawnKindDef or a XenotypeDef any more, so both
    operations had become silent no-ops.

    WHAT IT TOUCHES NOW, and why it is still needed at all:

      RimMandrake_Jawa        already `MandrakeJawa` 999   — nothing to do
      RimMandrake_JawaTribal  already `MandrakeJawa` 999   — nothing to do
      RimMandrakeJawa_Kind    `RimMandrakeJawa` 1.0        — 🔴 THE WRONG ONE

    ⚠️ TWO Jawa xenotypes ship from `mandrake.starwarsraces` and they are not the
    same thing: `MandrakeJawa` carries **35** genes and is the owner's hand-built
    set; `RimMandrakeJawa` carries **24** and is generator output. They share the
    label "Jawa", so the wrong one is invisible in play — you would have to count
    genes on a pawn to catch it. And `RimMandrakeJawa_Kind` is
    `defaultFactionDef PlayerColony`: it is the PLAYER'S Jawa.

    🔑 IT IS PATCHED HERE RATHER THAN FIXED AT SOURCE because
    `Defs/PawnKindDefs/RimMandrakePawnKinds.xml` is written by
    `gen_races_mod.py` — a hand edit there is erased by the next generator run.

    ⚠️ THE XENOTYPE IS THE ELEMENT NAME, NOT A VALUE. `xenotypeChances` is a
    def-keyed dictionary, so there is no text node to edit and the whole block is
    replaced. A `PatchOperationReplace` aimed at a `<li>` or at a value matches
    nothing here.

    Conditional, so a generator change degrades to a no-op rather than an error.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="RimMandrakeJawa_Kind"]/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances/RimMandrakeJawa</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="RimMandrakeJawa_Kind"]/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances</xpath>
      <value>
        <xenotypeChances>
          <MandrakeJawa>1.0</MandrakeJawa>
        </xenotypeChances>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
